<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Offers drop on basis switch.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Offers drop on basis switch.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash soymeal offers fell by $6.00 to $8.00 a ton as several U.S. dealers switched basis offers to the CBOT September soymeal contract without fully compensating for the $35.00 CBOT August-to-September premium, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers who continued to offer soymeal against the CBOT August reduced those values $3.00 to $5.00 per ton because of light demand.</p>
<p>Despite the drop in cash prices, business remained slow. Dealers said buyer interest may increase later Tuesday on belief that product was needed for prompt shipment.</p>
<p>Several soybean processing plants were down this week for routine maintenance, but dealers said soymeal supplies appear to be sufficient for the light demand.  </p>
